skill: caption-writer
version: 1.0.0
description: Scenario tests for caption-writer. A run passes only when every item in 'expect' is satisfied. Written before the skill body (test-first).
evals[8]:
  - name, input, expect
  - happy-path-instagram-saves, Write an Instagram caption for this photo of our team shipping a feature. Goal is saves., "reads brand-profile.md and voice.md before writing|writes a first line that hooks within Instagram's ~125-char preview cutoff|the body pays off the hook and is on-voice (fingerprint hit, 'never' list respected)|exactly one CTA, matched to the saves goal|uses a handful of relevant hashtags, not a wall, placed correctly|delivers 2-3 distinct options and recommends one with a rationale"
  - reads-foundation-and-guardrails, Caption this., loads voice.md and brand-profile.md|uses no exclamation marks and does not use 'excited'|does not write a hard-sell CTA|asks for platform/goal if not provided (at most 1-2 questions)
  - platform-adaptation, "Give me this same post as an Instagram caption, a LinkedIn post, and an X post.", "does NOT paste the same caption across all three|adapts the first line, length, hashtags, and CTA to each platform's mechanics|Instagram routes any link to 'link in bio'; X uses 0-2 hashtags; LinkedIn formats for dwell|each version still sounds like the same brand voice"
  - goal-drives-structure, "Write two captions for this post — one to get comments, one to drive clicks.", "the comments version ends on a genuine, low-effort question or open loop|the clicks version teases value and uses a traffic CTA appropriate to the platform|structure and CTA visibly differ based on the goal|each has only one CTA"
  - complements-not-describes, Caption for a photo of latte art at our cafe., "does NOT merely describe what's in the photo|adds an angle, story, or hook the image alone doesn't convey|first line earns attention rather than narrating the visual"
  - thin-input-asks-minimal, write a caption, "asks at most 1-2 essential questions (platform, goal) rather than a long form|does not invent brand specifics not in the profile|proceeds to a usable draft once it has enough"
  - no-link-platform-cta, Write an Instagram feed caption to drive people to our new blog post., recognizes links aren't clickable in IG feed captions|routes the CTA to 'link in bio' rather than writing a clickable-link CTA|still makes the click feel worth it
  - first-line-quality, Caption for our product launch., "does NOT open with 'We're thrilled/excited to announce'|leads with the benefit or a hook, not fanfare|first line creates curiosity, stakes, or recognition within the cutoff"
